  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Group Cash Transfer (GCT): Enhancing Community Agency for Localized Humanitarian</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to provide financial resources, strengthen the capacity and enhance the agency of the grassroot community groups in hard -to -reach areas to confront hazards and respond to their communities&apos; needs. Given that Group Cash Transfer (GCT) initiatives are locally led and decisions on their priority needs rests with each community group on the area it is difficult to predict the specific sectors (food security, livelihoods, water &amp; sanitation, Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR)/climate change, protection and early recovery) the projects will target. The project will benefit at least 28 community groups covering at least its 345 members (15 per group in Yemen for 13 groups and 10 per group in Lebanon for 15 groups) directly via the Group Cash Transfer and capacity enhancement activities and interventions in the two countries. These groups will have a role in leading and coordinating response members benefitting themselves and additionally about 12,000 individuals from the GCT initiatives. Again, as the GCT initiatives are decided by the GCT recipient groups themselves, it is difficult to predict the exact number of households each GCT initiative will target and benefit. However, the project will ensure at least 50% of the beneficiaries are women.</narrative>
  </description>
